 "variantC_note": "Variant C uses variant B's constants with the ITERATED dichotomy: case 2 lands in box(rho_B(r)); if rho_B(r) < r the same dichotomy re-applies at the smaller radius and the iterates fall to a fixed point x* ~ 1e-57 << r_N, so A22 finishes.  Condition: rho_B(r) < r.  NEITHER B NOR C IMPLIES THE OTHER: below r_N, C (rho < r) is STRICTER than B (rho <= r_N); above r_N it is the weaker one.  Since every radius certified here is below r_N, C buys nothing for v1 -- its refined crossover 2.75e-4 is SMALLER than the 3.5e-4 of B.  The iteration is what makes the v2 certificates work (m2b_global.py, h ~ 1.2e-3 > r_N), and it is recorded here for completeness and to correct the record: the sound condition is the DISJUNCTION B or C (variant BC), and for v1 that disjunction equals B.",
